arehouse-format stores offering more than 30,000 products in store and 1 million products online in the US, Canada, and Mexico. Its stores offer building materials, home improvement products, lawn and garden products, and decor products and provide various services, including home improvement installation services and tool and equipment rentals. The acquisition of Interline Brands in 2015 allowed Home Depot to enter the MRO business, which has been expanded through the tie-up with HD Supply (2020). The 2024 tie-up with SRS will help grow professional demand in roofing, pool, and landscaping projects, while the 2025 purchase of GMS will lift building product sales through 1,340 distribution locations. \n\nMorningstar• last month","title":"The Home Depot, Inc. (HD) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/HD/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LOW/","text":"Lowe's Companies, Inc. (LOW) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance\n\n# Lowe's Companies, Inc. (LOW)\n\n 198.68 -5.69 (-2.78%) \n\n At close: October 23 at 4:01:51 PM EDT \n\n 202.76 +4.08 (+2.05%) \n\nAfter hours: October 23 at 5:37:33 PM EDT \n\n## Trading disclosure \n\nLOW\n\n202.76 + 4.08 + 2.05% \n\n 1D -2.78% 5D +0.66% 1M +3.83% 6M -19.41% YTD -17.61% 1Y -18.53% 5Y -13.15% All +42.63K% \n\n## What's happening with LOW?\n\n6m ago\n\nLowe’s is balancing Pro customer growth and digital expansion against weak do-it-yourself demand and compressed margins. Management lowered fiscal 2026 expectations, while analysts expect another year-over-year earnings decline before the November results. The current regular-session move is down 2.78%.\n\n How much upside do analysts see from LOW's $204.4 price? What notable LOW insider transactions have been filed recently? What factors are driving LOW's 33% gross margin pressure? What's behind LOW's 2.78% regular-session drop? How is LOW balancing Pro growth with weak DIY demand? \n\n## Lowe's Companies, Inc. Overview Home Improvement Retail / Consumer Cyclical\n\nLowe's Companies, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a home improvement retailer in the United States and Canada. It provides a line of products for construction, maintenance, repair, remodeling, and decorating. The company also offers home improvement products, such as appliances, seasonal and outdoor living, lumber, lawn and garden, kitchens and bath, hardware, building materials, millwork, paint, rough plumbing, tools, electrical, flooring, and décor. In addition, it provides installation services through independent contractors in various product categories; and extended protection plans and repair services. Further, the company provides design, distribution, and installation services for interior surface finishes to home builders and property managers. It sells its national brand-name merchandise and private brand products to professional customers, individual homeowners, and renters. The company serves its products through Lowes.com website, mobile applications, retail home improvement stores and outlet stores, and its branches. Lowe's Companies, Inc. was founded in 1921 and is based in Mooresville, North Carolina.\n\ncorporate.lowes.com \n\n300,000\n\n### Full Time Employees\n\nJanuary 30\n\n### Fiscal Year Ends\n\nConsumer Cyclical \n\n### Sector\n\nHome Improvement Retail \n\n### Industry\n\n## Performance Overview \n\nTrailing total returns as of 10/23/2026, which may include dividends or other distributions. Benchmark is S&P 500 (^GSPC) .\n\n### YTD Return\n\nLOW 15.80% \n\nS&P 500 (^GSPC) 11.37%\n\n### 1-Year Return\n\nLOW 16.74% \n\nS&P 500 (^GSPC) 13.14%\n\n### 3-Year Return\n\nLOW 12.70% \n\nS&P 500 (^GSPC) 80.78%\n\n### 5-Year Return\n\nLOW 4.06% \n\nS&P 500 (^GSPC) 67.74%\n\n### Earnings Per Share \n\n### Revenue vs. Earnings \n\nQ2 FY27\n\nRevenue 25.96B\n\nEarnings 2.4B\n\nProfit Margin 9.24%\n\nQ3\n\nFY26\n\nQ4\n\nFY26\n\nQ1\n\nFY27\n\nQ2\n\nFY27\n\n0 \n\n5B \n\n